<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Launcher icon foreground: "Espiral" — one unbroken stroke coiling inward, constancy as the
    same small turn taken again.

    Authored on the 108x108 adaptive-icon viewport. Every arc is an exact semicircle, and the
    stroked extents stay inside the 66dp safe circle (centre 54,54 / radius 33), so no launcher
    mask — circle, squircle, rounded square — can clip the coil.

    android:strokeLineCap="round" is load-bearing: a butt cap squares off the coil's two free ends
    against the spiral's curvature and changes the drawing.

    Geometry constraint, learned the hard way: the radii step by 6.5 per half-turn, so adjacent
    turns sit 13 apart, and the 8-wide stroke reaches 4 either side of its centreline. That leaves
    a clean 5-wide gap. The first attempt used a pitch of 6 under a stroke of 9, so consecutive
    turns overlapped by 3 and welded into a solid disc with a notch — no spiral at any size, not
    just small ones. Any future change to the stroke must keep stroke < pitch.

    Two turns, not two and a half: a stroke this heavy cannot fit more inside the safe circle.

    Colour is ConstanzaColors.ACCENT_ARGB (#E8A860) over ConstanzaColors.BACKGROUND_ARGB.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M26,54 A28,28 0 0 1 82,54 A21.5,21.5 0 0 1 39,54 A15,15 0 0 1 69,54 A8.5,8.5 0 0 1 52,54"
        android:strokeColor="#E8A860"
        android:strokeWidth="8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round" />
</vector>
